/**
 * Locally authored CMS content, layered over `lib/cms.json`.
 *
 * `cms.json` is a snapshot regenerated by `pnpm cms`, so editing it directly
 * loses the edit on the next export -- the same reason artwork is overridden in
 * `app/globals.css` rather than in `framer/`. This is that idea for text: the
 * snapshot stays exactly as Framer produced it, and everything written here is
 * applied on top of it when `lib/cms.ts` builds the exported collections.
 *
 * The right long-term home for any of this is the Framer CMS itself. Move an
 * entry there, run `pnpm cms`, and delete it from this file.
 *
 * ---
 *
 * Field ids, not field names, are what reach the generated components: unframer
 * emits each binding as a module-level `var <fieldId><pageId>`, and
 * `__bindCmsFields` writes to those. The table below is the mapping for the
 * Program collection, read out of `cms.json` and checked against the ids the
 * generated files actually bind -- every id here appears in a
 * `framer/program-detail-section-*.jsx`. `lib/cms.ts` writes both the id and the
 * human name so server components (`generateMetadata`) and the rendered page
 * cannot disagree.
 */
